      "writtenOn": "2023-08-11T21:30:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "A RW lock performs better than a simple lock / synchronized block only if there is high contention on the lock and a high count of concurrent readers.\nI think this is unlikely to happen on a phone given the existing core count.\nIt might be simpler to just store the reverse mapping in a ConcurrentHashMap\u003cString, CopyOnWriteArraySet\u003e. This is fully thread-safe for all operations that you care about.",
      "revId": "2b30583f9aaf9795612db23d6d36056d85ae2c4e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
